From 7b19442b62b5ccd8eebc7e13da57b01cb0c418d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neo <65333514+neow021@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:49:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(feishu): open a topic for group replies and follow it
 without @mention

Two opt-in switches under platforms.feishu.extra, overridable per chat on a
group_rules entry:

- thread_reply: a top-level group message that triggers the bot is answered in a
  new topic. A short in-thread acknowledgement opens the topic before the turn
  runs, so the first turn already belongs to the topic's session.
- thread_follow: inside a topic this bot owns, follow-ups need no @mention. A
  message that @mentions someone else is left to them; the group policy still
  applies.

Ownership is the first bot-authored message in the topic, read from Feishu and
cached, so it survives restarts and a bot @mentioned once in another bot's topic
does not take it over. The behaviour lives in a new feishu_topic_follow sibling;
_fetch_last_message_in_thread moves there with it to keep the facade shrinking.
